Subject: Post-AGI research memo =E2=80=94 11 Sep 2026
To: tradesprior@gmail.com

Research memo for informational purposes only.

Key new findings:

1) Calibration debt: autonomous physical systems increase the number
of sensors and instruments whose calibration must remain trustworthy
over time. Recent robotics research shows calibration drift can become
a safety-critical attack surface, while Transcat reported Q1 FY2027
revenue +22% and service revenue +27%.

2) Cross-world casting collision: aerospace, defense and AI power
generation are bidding for the same constrained precision-casting
capacity. GE Aerospace agreed on Sep. 8 to acquire Consolidated
Precision Products for $11.75B specifically to address casting
bottlenecks; Doncasters reported Q2 aerospace revenue +47% and
industrial gas turbine revenue +42%.

3) Ceramic-core gating layer: Morgan Advanced Materials explicitly
says it is expanding ceramic-core capacity for turbine blades as
engine complexity rises. H1 2026 Technical Ceramics revenue grew 7.8%;
energy demand included industrial gas turbines serving data centers.
This is a third-order input beneath the already-visible casting
bottleneck.

4) Inspection-memory scarcity: as generic AI defect detection
improves, the scarce data may shift toward rare failures, degradation
histories and false-positive/false-negative cases. ESAB completed its
Eddyfi acquisition in June, adding recurring inspection and monitoring
exposure across aerospace, nuclear, energy and infrastructure.

5) Manufacturing-slot option value: long lead times turn future
production slots into economically valuable rights. Current 2026
procurement data still shows multi-quarter to multi-year lead times
for switchgear, transformers and large generators, with projects
reserving capacity well before site mobilization.

New kernel variables: calibration_debt, cross_world_collision_score,
qualification_time, design_complexity_multiplier,
negative_data_density, failure_history_uniqueness, slot_option_value.

Sources include arXiv 2608.28778 and 2601.16638; GE Aerospace/Reuters
Sep. 8=E2=80=939; Doncasters Q2 2026; Morgan Advanced Materials H1 2026;
ESAB/Eddyfi; Transcat Q1 FY2027.
